            <ArticleTitle>The coronary: &quot;will I have another?&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>951-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Awareness by medical practitioners of the need to keep their patients adequately informed of their conditions is of paramount importance in caring for those people who have had a myocardial infarction. This includes a realization that these people have questions to be answered at all stages of the illness, from the initial contact when in pain, throughout the hospital admission, and during rehabilitation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
